\title{zupmxode: Population Pharmacokinetic and Pharmacodynamic Simulation Without a Compiler}
\description{
Simulates population pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic models written in a subset of the 'rxode2' model language over 'NONMEM'-style event records, with no C compiler on the machine. Models are parsed in R and compiled to native code through 'MIR', or run by its interpreter where native code cannot be made. Closed-form compartment models are solved exactly, linear systems by a matrix exponential, and the rest by 'LSODA' or Dormand-Prince; subjects are solved in parallel with 'OpenMP'.
}
